{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>When the Most High gave nations their inheritance.</b> The commentators said: concerning the generation of the Dispersion, when all the earth was scattered — for then HaShem decreed that the land of the seven nations would belong to Israel, and that it would suffice for their number; therefore, 'according to the number of the children of Israel.'" "<b>He established.</b> Some say it is a noun, like 'the one who did not know' [הנה לא ידעתי]. And some say it is a future-tense verb in place of a past-tense verb, like 'they made a calf at Horeb' [יעשו עגל בחורב]. But the correct view in my eyes is that 'ask your father' is an allusion for the discerning, and likewise 'your elders.' The meaning is like 'which YHWH your Elohim apportioned,' for every portion below has a corresponding portion above." "And the meaning of <b>according to the number of the children of Israel</b> is as our Sages, may their memory be blessed, said: that the form of Jacob our father is engraved on the Throne of Glory. And it is a great sod, and the proof is 'HaShem's portion is His people.' And this is the great superiority, that He did not do so for any nation; therefore He said, 'Is this how you repay YHWH, O foolish and unwise people' — who fell from his rank through his folly. And this is the meaning of 'your father acquired you,' for He acquired him for His glory, and 'He will instruct him' — as explained, like the deed of a father with his son."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:52.683240416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}